\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Performance profiles of the tested cache algorithms. The y-axis shows the percentage of queries executing within a factor (x-axis) of the fastest algorithm. Curves closer to the top-left indicate better overall performance. The y-intercept ($x=1$) shows how often an algorithm is the outright fastest, while the rightward trajectory demonstrates robustness (e.g., $x=2, y=80\%$ means 80\% of queries execute within twice the fastest time). From the figure, we observe that all caching-based approaches outperform the no-cache baseline.}}{8}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:global_cache_performance}{{2}{8}{Performance profiles of the tested cache algorithms. The y-axis shows the percentage of queries executing within a factor (x-axis) of the fastest algorithm. Curves closer to the top-left indicate better overall performance. The y-intercept ($x=1$) shows how often an algorithm is the outright fastest, while the rightward trajectory demonstrates robustness (e.g., $x=2, y=80\%$ means 80\% of queries execute within twice the fastest time). From the figure, we observe that all caching-based approaches outperform the no-cache baseline}{figure.2}{}}
